    {
      "id": "qlbr1ck",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "HIGH COURT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Constitution provides specific provisions for the composition, appointment, qualifications, tenure, and removal of High Court judges.",
        "Under Article 226, High Courts possess writ jurisdiction for the enforcement of fundamental rights and for any other legal purpose.",
        "Article 227 confers supervisory jurisdiction to High Courts over all subordinate courts and tribunals within their territorial jurisdiction.",
        "As a Court of Record (Article 215), the High Court's judgments are recorded for perpetual memory and it holds the power to punish for contempt."
      ],
      "id": "hidrfw3"
    },
