    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 226 confers a broader writ jurisdiction on High Courts than Article 32 does on the Supreme Court, as High Courts can issue writs for legal rights beyond fundamental rights.",
        "High Courts derive their status as a Court of Record and power to punish for contempt from Article 215.",
        "Supervisory power over subordinate courts under Article 227 extends to both administrative and judicial superintendence."
      ],
      "id": "qdwik6v"
